            {
              "id": "CVE-2018-18064",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "cairo: Stack-based buffer overflow via parsing of crafted WebKitGTK+ document"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "cairo through 1.15.14 has an out-of-bounds stack-memory write during processing of a crafted document by WebKitGTK+ because of the interaction between cairo-rectangular-scan-converter.c (the generate and render_rows functions) and cairo-image-compositor.c (the _cairo_image_spans_and_zero function)."
