            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-13608",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "curl: curl: Authentication bypass in OpenLDAP SASL negotiation via Man-in-the-Middle (MITM) attack"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw in the libcurl SASL negotiation for LDAP authentication allows an\nincomplete handshake sequence to be misinterpreted as a successful\ncryptographic verification. An attacker executing a Man-in-the-Middle (MITM)\nattack can inject a premature or shortcut response that bypasses complete peer\nvalidation."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-13608",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-13608\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libcurl4t64\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-13608](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-13608)\nA flaw in the libcurl SASL negotiation for LDAP authentication allows an\nincomplete handshake sequence to be misinterpreted as a successful\ncryptographic verification. An attacker executing a Man-in-the-Middle (MITM)\nattack can inject a premature or shortcut response that bypasses complete peer\nvalidation.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-13608**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|libcurl4t64||[CVE-2026-13608](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-13608)|\n\nA flaw in the libcurl SASL negotiation for LDAP authentication allows an\nincomplete handshake sequence to be misinterpreted as a successful\ncryptographic verification. An attacker executing a Man-in-the-Middle (MITM)\nattack can inject a premature or shortcut response that bypasses complete peer\nvalidation."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
