            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-19931",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "curl: libcurl: Information disclosure via incorrect connection reuse with Negotiate authentication"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw in libcurl makes it wrongly reuse an HTTP connection setup for a given\nhostname using Negotiate authentication, when the initial request is done\nusing empty credentials. This can make user B's request get sent over user A's\npreviously authenticated connection."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-19931",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-19931\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libcurl4t64\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-19931](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-19931)\nA flaw in libcurl makes it wrongly reuse an HTTP connection setup for a given\nhostname using Negotiate authentication, when the initial request is done\nusing empty credentials. This can make user B's request get sent over user A's\npreviously authenticated connection.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-19931**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|libcurl4t64||[CVE-2026-19931](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-19931)|\n\nA flaw in libcurl makes it wrongly reuse an HTTP connection setup for a given\nhostname using Negotiate authentication, when the initial request is done\nusing empty credentials. This can make user B's request get sent over user A's\npreviously authenticated connection."
              },
              "properties": {
