            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-82209",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "curl: libcurl: Information disclosure via improper Public Suffix List boundary check"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When libpsl support is enabled, libcurl fails to enforce the Public Suffix\nList boundary check when processing a `Set-Cookie` header where the `Domain`\nattribute explicitly matches an origin host that is itself a public suffix\n(e.g., `Domain=co.uk` set by `co.uk`).\n\nInstead of coercing it into a strict host-only cookie, libcurl saves the\ncookie with wildcard domain scope (`.co.uk`). Consequently, the cookie is\ninappropriately included in subsequent outbound requests or HTTP redirects to\narbitrary sibling subdomains under the same public suffix (e.g.,\n`attacker.co.uk`)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-82209",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-82209\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libcurl4t64\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-82209](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-82209)\nWhen libpsl support is enabled, libcurl fails to enforce the Public Suffix\nList boundary check when processing a `Set-Cookie` header where the `Domain`\nattribute explicitly matches an origin host that is itself a public suffix\n(e.g., `Domain=co.uk` set by `co.uk`).\n\nInstead of coercing it into a strict host-only cookie, libcurl saves the\ncookie with wildcard domain scope (`.co.uk`). Consequently, the cookie is\ninappropriately included in subsequent outbound requests or HTTP redirects to\narbitrary sibling subdomains under the same public suffix (e.g.,\n`attacker.co.uk`).",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-82209**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|libcurl4t64||[CVE-2026-82209](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-82209)|\n\nWhen libpsl support is enabled, libcurl fails to enforce the Public Suffix\nList boundary check when processing a `Set-Cookie` header where the `Domain`\nattribute explicitly matches an origin host that is itself a public suffix\n(e.g., `Domain=co.uk` set by `co.uk`).\n\nInstead of coercing it into a strict host-only cookie, libcurl saves the\ncookie with wildcard domain scope (`.co.uk`). Consequently, the cookie is\ninappropriately included in subsequent outbound requests or HTTP redirects to\narbitrary sibling subdomains under the same public suffix (e.g.,\n`attacker.co.uk`)."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-19617",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "libdm: lvm2: libdm: Denial of Service via uncontrolled recursion in config parser"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in libdm. A local attacker could craft a malicious Logical Volume Manager (LVM) metadata configuration with deeply nested structures. This could lead to uncontrolled recursion in the libdm configuration file parser, exhausting the stack and causing any LVM command reading the metadata to crash. This vulnerability results in a Denial of Service (DoS) for affected systems."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-19617",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-19617\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libdevmapper1.02.1\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-19617](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-19617)\nA flaw was found in libdm. A local attacker could craft a malicious Logical Volume Manager (LVM) metadata configuration with deeply nested structures. This could lead to uncontrolled recursion in the libdm configuration file parser, exhausting the stack and causing any LVM command reading the metadata to crash. This vulnerability results in a Denial of Service (DoS) for affected systems.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-19617**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|libdevmapper1.02.1||[CVE-2026-19617](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-19617)|\n\nA flaw was found in libdm. A local attacker could craft a malicious Logical Volume Manager (LVM) metadata configuration with deeply nested structures. This could lead to uncontrolled recursion in the libdm configuration file parser, exhausting the stack and causing any LVM command reading the metadata to crash. This vulnerability results in a Denial of Service (DoS) for affected systems."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
