            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-27622",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "openexr: OpenEXR: Arbitrary code execution via integer overflow in EXR file processing"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "OpenEXR provides the specification and reference implementation of the EXR file format, an image storage format for the motion picture industry. In CompositeDeepScanLine::readPixels, per-pixel totals are accumulated in vector\u003cunsigned int\u003e total_sizes for attacker-controlled large counts across many parts, total_sizes[ptr] wraps modulo 2^32.  overall_sample_count is then derived from wrapped totals and used in samples[channel].resize(overall_sample_count). Decode pointer setup/consumption proceeds with true sample counts, and write operations in core unpack (generic_unpack_deep_pointers) overrun the undersized composite sample buffer. This vulnerability is fixed in v3.2.6, v3.3.8, and v3.4.6."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-27622",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-27622\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libopenexr-3-1-30\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-27622](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-27622)\nOpenEXR provides the specification and reference implementation of the EXR file format, an image storage format for the motion picture industry. In CompositeDeepScanLine::readPixels, per-pixel totals are accumulated in vector\u003cunsigned int\u003e total_sizes for attacker-controlled large counts across many parts, total_sizes[ptr] wraps modulo 2^32.  overall_sample_count is then derived from wrapped totals and used in samples[channel].resize(overall_sample_count). Decode pointer setup/consumption proceeds with true sample counts, and write operations in core unpack (generic_unpack_deep_pointers) overrun the undersized composite sample buffer. This vulnerability is fixed in v3.2.6, v3.3.8, and v3.4.6.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-27622**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|libopenexr-3-1-30||[CVE-2026-27622](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-27622)|\n\nOpenEXR provides the specification and reference implementation of the EXR file format, an image storage format for the motion picture industry. In CompositeDeepScanLine::readPixels, per-pixel totals are accumulated in vector\u003cunsigned int\u003e total_sizes for attacker-controlled large counts across many parts, total_sizes[ptr] wraps modulo 2^32.  overall_sample_count is then derived from wrapped totals and used in samples[channel].resize(overall_sample_count). Decode pointer setup/consumption proceeds with true sample counts, and write operations in core unpack (generic_unpack_deep_pointers) overrun the undersized composite sample buffer. This vulnerability is fixed in v3.2.6, v3.3.8, and v3.4.6."
              },
