              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "libsoup: libsoup: HTTP header injection and response splitting via CRLF injection in Content-Type header"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in libsoup. An attacker controlling the value used to set the Content-Type header can inject a Carriage Return Line Feed (CRLF) sequence due to improper input sanitization in the `soup_message_headers_set_content_type()` function. This vulnerability allows for the injection of arbitrary header-value pairs, potentially leading to HTTP header injection and response splitting attacks."
